# Managed by the website repo (ops/caddy/umami.caddy, #948). ops/install-umami.sh fills in the
# host, the port and the HSTS file's path, copies the result to
# /etc/caddy/sprecher-east-umami.caddy and imports it from the Caddyfile, but only after Umami's
# default admin password has been replaced (until then ops/caddy/umami-closed.caddy is in its
# place). Change it in the repo, not on the server.
#
# Umami has its own address because the prebuilt image cannot run under a path (BASE_PATH is
# fixed when the image is built). Caddy gets the certificate and redirects plain HTTP by itself.
# The HSTS rule is the site's own file (ops/caddy/hsts.caddy), so there is one definition of it.
__UMAMI_HOST__ {
	import __HSTS_FILE__
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:__UMAMI_PORT__
}
